  "name": "Calendar links syntax for chats (jump to calendar entry)",
  "pinned": false,
  "is_template": false,
  "description": "Add a link syntax usable in chat messages (and task/project descriptions) that points to a calendar entry, so clicking it opens the calendar on that entry.\n\nRequirements:\n- Syntax candidates: `cal://<entry_id>`, `calendar:<entry_id>`, or `[label](cal://id?date=YYYY-MM-DD)`. Support scheduled tasks (projected source='task' entries) and stored events. For tasks, `task://<chat_id>` should resolve to the projected calendar occurrence.\n- Client: markdown renderer must turn the syntax into an anchor that routes to the calendar view with the entry selected and the date in focus (month view + open detail panel).\n- API: expose a resolver endpoint that accepts an entry id (or task chat id + date) and returns the occurrence/event, its calendar, start/end and a deep-link URL.\n- Unresolvable entries must render as plain text with a tooltip, never a dead link.\n- Tests for the parser and the resolver.\n\nAcceptance: a chat message containing the link opens the calendar at the entry when clicked.",
